     1	# Goblin updater
     2	[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache%202.0-blue.svg)](LICENSE.txt)
     3	
     4	The Goblin updater formulates the dependency update problem as a multi-objective optimization problem. This approach allows for the update of dependencies with a global perspective, considering all direct and indirect dependencies. It also enables developers to specify their preferences regarding the quality factors they want to maximize and the costs of updating they want to minimize. The update problem is encoded as a linear program whose solution is an optimal update strategy that aligns with developer priorities and minimizes incompatibilities.
     5	
     6	An example of usage of this tool is available here: TODO
     7	
     8	## Requirements
     9	- Java 17
    10	- An active Neo4j database containing the Maven Central dependency graph available here: https://zenodo.org/records/11104819
    11	- A Goblin weaver API available here: https://github.com/Goblin-Ecosystem/goblinWeaver
    12	
    13	## Source code structure
    14	
    15	- client : clients
    16	- updater : Goblin updater
    17	  - api : API for the updater
    18	  - impl : implementation of the API
    19	  - helpers : helpers using the API
    20	- util : utilities that are not specific to Goblin updater
    21	
    22	## JAR generation
    23	
    24	```sh
    25	mvn clean package
    26	```
    27	
    28	## Execution
    29	
    30	To run Goblin Updater, you have first to run the Goblin Weaver server. More information [here](https://github.com/Goblin-Ecosystem/goblinWeaver).
    31	
    32	1. run Neo4J and launch the graph database for the ecosystem
    33	
    34	2. run Goblin Weaver server in a first terminal
    35	    ```sh
    36	    java -Dneo4jUri="bolt://localhost:7687/" -Dneo4jUser="neo4j" -Dneo4jPassword="goblindb" -jar ./target/goblinWeaver-1.0.0.jar noUpdate
    37	    ```
    38	
    39	3. run Goblin Updater in a second terminal
    40	    ```sh
    41	    java -DweaverUrl=<WEAVER URL> -DprojectPath=<PROJECT TO ANALYSE> -DconfFile=<CONFIGURATION FILE> -jar <JAR FILE>
    42	    ```
    43	
    44	Windows example:
    45	
    46	```sh
    47	java -DweaverUrl="http://localhost:8080" -DprojectPath="C:\Users\Bob\MyProgram" -DconfFile=".\gUpdaterConfig.yml" -jar .\goblinUpdater-1.0.0-jar-with-dependencies.jar
    48	```
    49	
    50	Linux / MacOS example:
    51	
    52	```sh
    53	java -DweaverUrl="http://localhost:8080" -DprojectPath="$HOME/MyProgram" -DconfFile="./gUpdaterConfig.yml" -jar .\goblinUpdater-1.0.0-jar-with-dependencies.jar
    54	```
    55	
    56	## Configuration files
    57	
    58	see the [template configuration file](gUpdaterConfig_TEMPLATE.yml)


