    11	- Cve dataset (dated May 07, 2024) available here: TODO Zenodo
    12	
    13	## Setup
    14	Download the goblin-updater jar "goblinUpdater-1.0.0-jar-with-dependencies.jar", and put it on the "updater" folder at the root of the project.
    15	
    16	## Run Dataset Generator
    17	1. Download the original dataset call "projects.zip" here: https://zenodo.org/record/4479015/
    18	2. Unzip the archive, it will be passed by argument.
    19	3. Choose "DatasetGenerator" at "experienceToRun" on the configuration.yml file at src/main/java/resources.
    20	4. Make sure Docker is running.
    21	5. run the "runDatasetGenerator.sh" script with the unziped projects folder path as argument.
    22	
    23	## Run experiments
    24	Among the experiments, "runUpdater" should be run first, with the others based on the results obtained by this one.
    25	Execution results will be accessible in a new "outfiles" folder at project root.
    26	To run one of the following experiments "compileAndTest", "naiveUpdate" or compareConfQualityAndCost, you need to put the results of the "runUpdater" experiment in a "results" folder in the project root.
    27	
    28	1. Run your Neo4j Maven Central dependency graph
    29	2. Run the Goblin Weaver API
    30	3. Make sure Docker is running.
    31	4. Choose the experiments to run on the configuration.yml file at src/main/java/resources.
    32	5. Put your Goblin Weaver API url on the configuration.yml file at src/main/java/resources.
    33	6. run the "run.sh" script.
    34	
    35	The results of the run will be present on a new folder call "outFiles".
    36	
    37	The experiments "compileAndTest" and "naiveUpdate" uses the results of the experiment "runUpdater".
    38	If you use this, you have to put the result of the "runUpdater" experiment on the "result" folder.
    39	


